  "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nMRV2 `draft_model` (`StandaloneARSpeculator`) with a MoE target and DP > 1 crashes at startup: the drafter passes the target's `num_tokens_across_dp` to its own forwards, which run a different number of tokens, and `DPMetadata.make` asserts.\n\nRelated: #56281 (same assert in DSpark, fixed by #54856), #56734 (dummy-run masking for EAGLE). Not a duplicate: no open or closed PR covers these fixes. #56136 touches the same dynamic-SD gate but not which managers capture per K.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fix the `draft_model` + MoE + DP > 1 startup crash (`AssertionError: 7168 1024`).\n- Port #56734's dummy-run `idx_mapping` masking to the standalone drafter, so idle DP ranks don't write draft KV through stale block tables.\n- Fix the draft prefill's `seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound`, which was one short.\n- Stop `DFlashCudaGraphManager` (DFlash/DFlash2/DSpark) capturing per-K FULL graphs under dynamic SD that it never dispatches.\n\n## Validation\n\nQwen3-30B-A3B target, Qwen3-0.6B draft, K=3, MRV2, H100s. GSM8K 5-shot, 1319 questions.\n\n| Config | GSM8K | Acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| DP=1, no spec | 0.889 | \u2014 |\n| DP=1, draft_model | 0.889 | 81.6% |\n| DP=2, draft_model, main | crash at startup | \u2014 |\n| DP=2, draft_model, this PR | 0.899 | 81.8% |\n\n- No sync warnings with `VLLM_GPU_SYNC_CHECK=warn` at DP=2.\n- Prefill bound: a temporary check found the actual draft `seq_lens` above the CPU bound on 539/549 prefills before, 0 after.\n- Idle-rank dummy batches: a tiny random-weight MoE at DP=2 with single and burst requests completes; main crashes.\n- `tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py`, `tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dynamic_sd_cug.py`, `tests/v1/cudagraph/test_cudagraph_manager.py`, `tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_block_table.py`: 56 passed. Both new tests fail on main.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Repro</summary>\n\n```bash\nVLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1 vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B --data-parallel-size 2 \\\n  --max-model-len 4096 --port 8001 \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"draft_model\",\"model\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":3}'\npython tests/evals/gsm8k/gsm8k_eval.py --port 8001\n```\n</details>\n\n## Details\n\n- **DP sync.** The draft prefill runs `num_tokens + num_reqs` tokens and each decode step `num_reqs`, so each syncs its own count via `dispatch_cg_and_sync_dp(need_eager=True)`: once for prefill, once before the decode loop. That adds two CPU all-reduces per `propose` at DP > 1. Reusing the target's sync (as the target-dependent drafters do) would mean padding eager attention metadata here, since the target sync only carries the max request count.\n- **Prefill bound.** The prefill kernel writes `seq_len + 1` per request for the correction token, so the prefill now passes `step=1`, as decode already does. FlashInfer TRTLLM prefill with FP8 KV and the sparse MLA backends size work from this bound.\n- **DFlash capture.** New `CudaGraphManager.dynamic_sd_query_lens = True`, set to `False` on `DFlashCudaGraphManager`.\n- **CI.** No CI step runs a MoE target with a draft model at DP=2; the e2e runs above were local.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>",
